13. API design
Organize the API by business responsibility.
Authentication and users
- POST /api/auth/register — register a user.
- POST /api/auth/login — authenticate.
- POST /api/auth/logout — log out or invalidate the session.
- GET /api/users/me — retrieve the logged-in user's profile.
- GET /api/admin/users — list users for authorized administrators.
- PATCH /api/admin/users/{user_id} — update an account or its status.
Clubs
- GET /api/clubs — retrieve permitted club information.
- POST /api/admin/clubs — create a club.
- PATCH /api/admin/clubs/{club_id} — update or deactivate a club.
Kit and availability
- GET /api/kit — retrieve kit information.
- GET /api/kit/items — retrieve equipment items and their status.
- GET /api/availability?date=... — retrieve available slots for a date.
Bookings
- POST /api/bookings — create a booking.
- GET /api/bookings — retrieve bookings visible to the current user.
- GET /api/bookings/{booking_id} — retrieve an authorized booking.
- POST /api/bookings/{booking_id}/cancel — cancel an eligible booking.
- GET /api/clubs/{club_id}/bookings — retrieve a club's bookings, with ownership checks.
Checkout, return, and inspection
- POST /api/bookings/{booking_id}/checkout — submit checkout information.
- POST /api/bookings/{booking_id}/return — submit return information.
- GET /api/bookings/{booking_id}/inspections — retrieve inspection history.
Incidents and notifications
- GET /api/incidents — retrieve incidents visible to the current user.
- POST /api/incidents — report an incident.
- POST /api/incidents/{incident_id}/recover — record recovery.
- POST /api/incidents/{incident_id}/replace — record replacement.
- POST /api/incidents/{incident_id}/resolve — resolve a verified incident.
- GET /api/notifications — retrieve the logged-in user's notifications.
- POST /api/notifications/{notification_id}/read — mark a notification as read.
Audit and health
- GET /api/admin/audit-logs — retrieve authorized audit history.
- GET /api/health — basic application health check.
These are proposed endpoints. Antigravity should implement them consistently and document the request and response formats. Use HTTP status codes appropriately, such as 401 for unauthenticated requests, 403 for forbidden actions, 404 for unavailable resources, and 409 for booking conflicts.
