16. Testing requirements
Antigravity should create automated tests for these scenarios before considering the project complete.
Booking tests
- A valid booking is created.
- An overlapping booking is rejected.
- A booking starting 14 minutes after the previous booking is rejected.
- A booking starting exactly 15 minutes later passes the gap check.
- A cancelled booking no longer blocks a time slot.
- An inactive club cannot create a booking.
- Invalid or past times are rejected.
- Two simultaneous conflicting requests cannot both succeed.
Authentication and authorization tests
- Valid credentials allow login.
- Invalid credentials are rejected.
- An unauthenticated user cannot access protected endpoints.
- A club representative cannot access another club's private booking.
- A club representative cannot perform checkout or resolve incidents.
- Only authorized administrators can manage roles.
Inspection and incident tests
- Checkout is blocked if a required item is missing.
- Checkout is blocked if a required item is unusable.
- An inspection cannot be completed while required item results are missing.
- Return inspection detects damaged or missing equipment.
- An incident marks affected future bookings at risk.
- Recovery or replacement does not automatically mark the entire kit ready if another item remains unusable.
- A cancelled booking cannot be checked out.
Notification and audit tests
- A booking confirmation is recorded after successful booking creation.
- A failed notification does not undo a committed booking.
- Retrying a notification does not unnecessarily duplicate it.
- Important admin and user actions create audit records.
