4. Required business rules
- There is one physical kit, KIT-001.
- Every booking has a start time and end time.
- End time must be later than start time.
- Reject past bookings and inactive-club booking requests.
- Prevent overlapping reservations.
- Enforce a 15-minute gap after the previous booking ends.
- If a booking ends at 3:00 PM, the next booking may start at 3:15 PM, provided all other rules pass.
- Exclude cancelled bookings from conflict checks.
- Prevent simultaneous conflicting booking requests using atomic database operations and appropriate concurrency control.
- Require inspection results for the camera, tripod, and microphone at checkout and return.
- Block handover if required equipment is missing or unusable.
- Do not assume the kit is ready just because 15 minutes have passed.
- Keep booking status separate from equipment status and booking risk.
- When equipment becomes unavailable, identify potentially affected future bookings, mark them at risk, and notify the appropriate users.
- Do not automatically cancel all affected bookings.
- Record cancellation reasons and important administrative actions.
